cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RAHN in research, cite this repository."
title: "RAHN: a stateful execution architecture for evolving networks"
abstract: >-
  RAHN models network state as a deterministic, content-addressed object: changes are
  explicit transitions, every candidate state passes a constitution of invariants
  before it can be committed, evolution uses branches with a fail-closed semantic
  merge, and execution is simulation-first. v1.0.0 is a stable architecture, not a
  production network controller. Source code is Apache-2.0; documentation,
  specification, and research materials are CC BY 4.0.
authors:
